{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"8956914907191afb9f226a7436c2a302b7047c92bd97493af3b82073ee750e69","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_d0fa879bf24dd998d1ac487b78cf4dc694d2879ad2640c17caa27f294d9674fb","overall_assessment":"The paper proposes a foundational experimental framework for evaluating out-of-distribution novelty generation, addressing a significant gap in the evaluation of generative models. By introducing a hold-out class setup and specific metrics, it provides a systematic approach to studying creativity in machine learning. The work is significant for the research community as it redefines the objective of generative models from in-distribution sampling to novelty generation, potentially influencing future research in this area. The experimental results demonstrate the applicability of the proposed metrics, although the scope is limited to MNIST and Google Fonts, which may restrict the generalizability of the findings.","paper_id":"ByEPMj5el","paper_identity_sha256":"11d3f3d5c6111466c833cbb71d34d8e13480d51fb8f8a00dd1efc439dd8fc0e1","prompt_identity_sha256":"a50b78fb6866ccc41e831edba1c46ae13727defddee8eb8071f1271a21adf337","raw_response_sha256":"341e0375f5c231d588f1d4943a5dea573dec05758b6e228a92e8ca7ac75277de","request_identity_sha256":"f1893d41f961b3310d3b6144c6072c64232ba678f3ae45633f2c367f6a1f98ec","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"SIGN","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"b1a57423ed0ad7f6034f1e0658bacac795fd735d74a1c49c22e1072de0235c87","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036","SRC-037","SRC-038","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper addresses a broadly important problem by proposing a new experimental framework for evaluating out-of-distribution novelty generation. This framework is likely to influence multiple research areas, including computational creativity and generative modeling, by providing a systematic way to study creativity in relation to knowledge acquisition. The work introduces a paradigm that may influence many researchers by redefining the objective of generative models from in-distribution sampling to novelty generation.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-BRD"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036","SRC-037","SRC-038","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper makes a significant contribution to the domain of computational creativity by providing a new experimental setup for evaluating the generative potential of models. The method outperforms existing approaches by addressing an important challenge in the field, which is the lack of a clear-cut evaluation process for out-of-distribution novelty generation. The domain-specific benchmarks used (MNIST and Google Fonts) are appropriate for the task, and the results demonstrate the applicability of the proposed metrics.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-DOM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036","SRC-037","SRC-038","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper reports substantial improvements over the state of the art by introducing a new experimental setup and metrics for evaluating out-of-distribution novelty generation. The improvements are consistent across various types of generative models, and the results are supported by appropriate statistical analysis. The paper demonstrates that the proposed metrics are effective in selecting good out-of-class generators, which is a significant advancement over previous work that lacked a clear evaluation process.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-SOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036","SRC-037","SRC-038","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper discusses the potential practical and societal ramifications of the work, including the benefits of studying creativity in machine learning and the risks of generating out-of-distribution novelty. The authors acknowledge the importance of human evaluation and the need for a clear-cut evaluation process. However, the paper does not extensively discuss the fairness, environmental impact, or accessibility of the proposed method, which could be areas for future work.","subdimension_id":"SIGN-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"392555bfa8bf5525d1925e2e41c381d6d278b0d2c3d13167201e0eae4b69d986","paper_id":"ByEPMj5el","paper_ordinal":67,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"341e0375f5c231d588f1d4943a5dea573dec05758b6e228a92e8ca7ac75277de","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"ByEPMj5el","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_